[TEXT] **ROOT CAUSE FOUND.** Router6's `nft list ruleset` FORWARD chain reveals an ACL on `eth2` (the r6_r3 uplink from router3):

```
chain FORWARD {
    iifname "eth2" ip saddr 172.16.10.0/24 ip daddr 172.18.51.1 tcp dport 80 counter accept
    iifname "eth2" meta l4proto tcp counter packets 0 drop
    iifname "eth2" meta l4proto udp counter packets 25 bytes 1500 drop   ← 25 pkts (traceroute probes)
    iifname "eth2" counter packets 24 bytes 2016 drop                    ← 24 pkts (ICMP pings)
}
```

This ACL **drops all TCP, UDP, and ICMP** arriving on router6's eth2 (the r6_r3 link from router3). Notably:
- The 25 UDP drops = our traceroute probes (matching traceroute `*` at hop 6)
- The 24 ICMP drops = our ping probes

